# 12. Display-Only Weight Rule

A product rule was identified during real OKR testing:

> **Weight = 0% means Display Only.**

The intended behavior is:

```text
Weight > 0%
    = scoring / weighted item

Weight = 0%
    = display-only item
    = does not contribute to scoring
```

This applies to Key Results.

An Objective with 0% weight may also represent a display-only objective if
that is consistent with the final validation implementation.

Weighted items must still satisfy the appropriate 100% aggregation rules.

For example:

```text
KR A     50%
KR B     50%
KR C      0%   ← Display Only
----------------
          100%
```

is valid.

This rule must be implemented deliberately in Builder validation and UI
language.

Do not silently weaken all weight validation.

